2. Do NOT upload these
Files

Reason

data/raw/*.fastq.gz

Large raw sequencing data

results/trimmed/*.fq.gz

Large intermediate reads

results/assembly/megahit/intermediate_contigs/

Intermediate assembly files

results/kraken2/*.kraken

Large classification output

results/biom/*.biom

Optional; TSV is enough for portfolio

logs/

Not necessary for the main portfolio

run_wms.sh.backup and .save files

Old script copies

requirements-resolved.txt

Temporary dependency snapshot

Database files

Too large; keep outside GitHub

3. Create your .gitignore
Run:

nano .gitignore

Paste:

data/raw/
results/trimmed/
results/assembly/megahit/intermediate_contigs/
results/kraken2/*.kraken
results/biom/*.biom
logs/
*.backup
*.save
*.save.*
__pycache__/
Save using Ctrl + O, Enter, Ctrl + X.

4. Add the selected files to Git
Run:

git add .gitignore config/ docker/ scripts/run_wms.sh scripts/pull_docker_images.sh

Then add the selected results:

git add results/assembly/megahit/final.contigs.fa
git add results/gene_prediction/genes.gff results/gene_prediction/proteins.faa
git add results/kraken2/Tetragonlairidipennis.report
git add results/bracken/Tetragonlairidipennis.bracken
git add results/cog_annotation/cog_classify.tsv results/cog_annotation/cog_count.tsv results/cog_annotation/*.png
git add results/biom/otu_table/OTU_TABLE.tsv
git add results/qc/raw/*.html results/qc/trimmed/*.html

5. Check and upload
git status

If the files look correct:

git commit -m "Add Docker-based WMS pipeline with analysis results"
git push -u origin main

Your Docker image stays on Docker Hub: kparate/wms-pipeline:1.0. GitHub will contain the Dockerfiles, scripts, configuration, and example outputs.

One important point: your current run_wms.sh must use the paths in config/config.sh correctly before you describe the pipeline as portable in your README.





data/raw/
results/trimmed/
results/assembly/megahit/intermediate_contigs/
results/kraken2/*.kraken
results/biom/*.biom
scripts/*.backup
scripts/*.save*
docker/bioinfo-tools/requirements-resolved.txt
